  <constraints>
    <constraint type="infrastructure">EC2 instance is t4g.small with 2GB RAM. Memgraph memory limit MUST be set to 512MB (--memory-limit=512) and container limit to 600M. Total system peak ~1.8GB. Monitor for OOM — may require upgrade to t4g.medium.</constraint>
    <constraint type="architecture">Memgraph is NOT the source of truth — wiki markdown files are. Memgraph is a disposable query accelerator rebuilt from wiki content. Data loss in Memgraph is recoverable but costly (re-embedding).</constraint>
    <constraint type="platform">EC2 runs Ubuntu 24.04 ARM64 (aarch64). All Docker images must support ARM64 architecture. Memgraph official image supports this.</constraint>
    <constraint type="networking">Memgraph ports (7687, 7444) should only be accessible from localhost (EC2 internal). Do NOT expose to public internet. The daemon connects locally.</constraint>
    <constraint type="persistence">Docker volume memgraph-data must persist across container restarts. Use named volume, not bind mount, for Docker-managed lifecycle.</constraint>
    <constraint type="operations">Container must use restart: unless-stopped so it survives EC2 reboots but can be manually stopped for maintenance.</constraint>
  </constraints>

